Z||000000||Cozmo||11-15-2001||05:26 AM||||Just got done installing another engine in an '86 GT auto.  The car runs good, ECM blows no codes but it has a weird starting problem.  When cold, it starts within 2 or 3 cranks (normal, like most other 2.8s) but when warm you need to crank it for about 2 seconds before it finally fires.  It then starts rough but finally smooths out in about 5 seconds.  It has new plugs, wires, cap&rotor, fuel and air filter.  I did a fuel pressure leakdown test, it starts out at about 40psi and after about 2 min drops to 20psi.  Is this normal?  Any ideas?<P>Thanks! <P>------------------<BR><B>BobC</B><BR><B>'85 2M6 Targa</B><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/targsig.jpg"> <BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTZ34||11-15-2001||09:32 AM||||No that is not normal, sounds like you have some leaky injectors.  That failure matches your syptoms of good cold starts but slow warm starts.  When warm the engine has to pump some air through it to clean out the gas buildup.  You may want to redo the leakdown and pinch off the return to make sure that the fuel regulator isn't what is leaking.  If it is not, then you need new injectors.  Injector cleaner/lube may help but I doubt it (I use the good STP stuff when I use it).  I replaced my injectors 1K mi ago and they had 156K on them.  That engine was overheated to the point that it needed an overhaul by the previous owner and I'm sure that contributed to their failure.<BR>GL||||reg||1
